    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0076",
      "sequence": 88,
      "meaning": "Śiva teaches sages in some places and elsewhere sings Rāma’s virtues. Though desireless, the compassionate Lord suffers from separation from his devotee. Much time passes and his love for Rāma’s feet grows ever new. Seeing Śaṅkara’s constant rule and unwavering line of devotion, grateful, merciful Rāma appears—an immense treasury of beauty, character and splendor. He praises Śiva repeatedly, saying no one else could sustain such a vow, consoles him in many ways, recounts Pārvatī’s birth and describes Girijā’s supremely pure deeds in detail. Rāma then asks Śiva, if he truly loves him, to go marry the mountain’s daughter and grant this request.",
