    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0077",
      "sequence": 89,
      "meaning": "Śiva replies that although marriage does not seem fitting, he cannot set aside his Lord’s word. He will place the command upon his head, for obeying is his highest duty. The speech of mother, father, teacher and master should be accepted as auspicious without deliberation, and Rāma is his supreme benefactor in every way. Pleased by Śaṅkara’s devotion-, discernment- and dharma-filled reply, Rāma tells him to preserve his vow while keeping this request in his heart. Rāma vanishes; Śaṅkara retains that form within. The Seven Sages arrive, and Śiva instructs them to test Pārvatī’s love, send Himālaya to bring her home and remove his doubt.",
