      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0078",
      "sequence": 90,
      "meaning": "The sages see Gaurī as austerity embodied and ask why she practices such severe penance, whom she worships and what she desires, urging her to tell them the truth. Speaking, she feels deeply embarrassed and says they will laugh at her foolishness: her obstinate mind rejects counsel and wants to raise a wall upon water; trusting Nārada’s word as true, she wishes to fly without wings. Such is her folly—she always desires Śiva as husband.",
