    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0080",
      "sequence": 92,
      "meaning": "The sages urge Pārvatī still to accept their advice: they have chosen Viṣṇu, a fine groom—beautiful, pure, gracious, joyful, faultless, a treasury of every virtue, Lakṣmī’s Lord and resident of Vaikuṇṭha. Bhavānī smiles: what they say accords with her mountain-born body, but her resolve will leave only when her body does. Even gold arising from stone does not abandon its nature when burned. She will not forsake Nārada’s word, whether her home thrives or is ruined; one who lacks faith in the teacher’s word cannot attain happiness or accomplishment even in a dream. Mahādeva may be a house of faults and Viṣṇu an abode of all virtues, yet one desires only the one in whom one’s mind delights.",
